      "summary": "Cancel pending close order",
      "description": "**Rate limit:** 20 requests per 60 seconds. This is a **shared quota** — the same budget is consumed by a group of related endpoints, so calling any of them reduces what is left for the others (you cannot call each at the full rate independently). Endpoints sharing this quota:\n- `DELETE /api/v1/trading/execution/limit-orders/{orderId}`\n- `DELETE /api/v1/trading/execution/market-open-orders/{orderId}`\n- `DELETE /api/v2/trading/execution/orders/{orderId}`\n- `DELETE /api/v3/trading/execution/orders/{orderId}`\n- `POST /api/v1/trading/execution/limit-orders`\n- `POST /api/v1/trading/execution/market-close-orders/positions/{positionId}`\n- `POST /api/v1/trading/execution/market-open-orders/by-amount`\n- `POST /api/v1/trading/execution/market-open-orders/by-units`\n- `POST /api/v2/trading/execution/orders`\n- `POST /api/v3/trading/execution/orders`\n\n---\n\nThis endpoint allows traders to cancel a previously placed market order for close before execution. If the order has already been processed, cancellation will not be possible. A 200 response confirms the cancellation request was received, not that the order was cancelled. Confirm with GET /api/v1/trading/info/real/close-orders/{orderId}, using the orderId of the close order you tried to cancel. If the DELETE response is lost (timeout or network error), do not resend the cancel - poll that GET endpoint with the same orderId. Units reported as executed in its positions[] array were closed before the cancel took effect; the remainder was not closed. No executed entries in positions[] means nothing was closed. Poll until statusID is terminal: 7 (CANCELED) = cancelled with nothing executed, 9 (CANCELED_PARTIALLY_FILLED) = cancelled after a partial fill (executed units in positions[]), 3 (FILLED) = fully executed before the cancel; 1, 2, 5, 6 and 11 are still pending.",
